      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a bathroom remodel usually take in Federal Way?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Project timelines depend on scope. Smaller updates can sometimes be completed in as little as one day, while a more complete streamlined remodel may take up to one week depending on layout, materials, and the amount of work involved."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What upgrades make the biggest difference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The most valuable upgrades usually include better storage, improved lighting, a more functional shower or tub area, and durable finishes. These changes improve daily comfort while also making the bathroom more practical and appealing over time.\u00a0"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a shower remodel enough, or should I plan a full bathroom renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A shower remodel may be enough if the main issue is the wet area. If layout, storage, and overall function need improvement, a full bathroom renovation is often the better long-term solution."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are slip-resistant floors worth adding to a bathroom remodel?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For many homeowners, yes. Slip-resistant flooring can improve safety and confidence without affecting the overall look of the bathroom. It is a practical upgrade that supports everyday comfort and usability."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does bathroom remodeling cost in Federal Way?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The cost of a bathroom remodel depends on the scope, materials, and level of finish. Entry-level projects typically range from 15,000 to 20,000, while an average bathroom remodel falls between 25,000 and 30,000. High-end renovations with premium materials and more complex work can range from 50,000 to 60,000."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a bathroom remodel improve home value?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. A well-executed bathroom remodel can improve both daily living and perceived home value. Buyers often respond to updated layouts, clean finishes, and practical improvements that make the space easier to use."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What should I ask about Federal Way building requirements before construction starts?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is important to ask what requirements may apply to your specific project scope. Because rules can vary based on the type of work, clarifying this early helps avoid delays and ensures smoother planning."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
